  Quote of the Week:

  Desierius Erasmus, Dutch scholar, 1521:
  "Let a King recall that to improve his realm is better than to increase 
his territory."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Winter gave way to fragrant spring, and Bradipo I prepared to carry out 
his urgent orders.  He travelled to Kiska.
  With the advent of the early summer season, Bradipo I cast a Tornado 
spell.  Magical tornadoes hit the defenders of Kiska.  The Tornado affected 
no armies in Kiska.
  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Bradipo I (whose 
alliances are too incompatible) and Kahn (#6), degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!
  With the advent of the late summer season Bradipo I's Skeletal Army spell 
fizzled and Bradipo I wound up covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  The sultry days of summer surrendered to the fall.  Bradipo I could not 
cast Part Sea on Khalturin because it is a non-flooded land hex.  So, 
Bradipo I worked on his White Magic but was frustrated in his efforts.
  During early winter, Bradipo I practiced his White Magic well, and even 
consulted a palm reader, but could not improve his skill in White Magic.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Bradipo I for this year.


  Bradipo I treated with his ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Bradipo I 
treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Bradipo I treated with his ally Prometeo 
(#5).  Bradipo I asked II Kahn (#6) to improve diplomatic relations with his 
great Kingdom, speaking at length of the great benefits of such an 
agreement.  After some deliberation, the offer was graciously accepted by 
Kahn.
  Bradipo I treated with his ally Giovanna (#7).  Bradipo I treated with his 
ally Circe (#8).  Bradipo I treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Bradipo I's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 0 gold in revenue.  1 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Bradipo I was left 
with 104 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Mortimer, Squire to Adele
To: Bradipo I

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season Adele prepared to quench her thirst 
for adventure.  Her attempted cast of the Tornado spell was unsuccessful.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Adele girded her weapon and 
entered the Cave warily.  Adele encountered the Renegade Swordsman.  Casting 
a Hand Of Death spell, Adele directed glowing, writhing strands of magic and 
began making squeezing motions with her hands.
  The Renegade Swordsman quickly moved into bow range.
  The Renegade Swordsman charged into melee range.  The unseen hands of 
Adele grasped his throat, choking the life out of the Renegade Swordsman and 
damaged the Renegade Swordsman, inflicting 2 damage points.  
The Renegade Swordsman summoned all his will and desperately thrust at his 
vaunted enemy and scorched Adele with 2 damage points.  Her spell was 
disrupted by the event.  Adele incanted the magic words for an Ice 
Suspension spell, but bit her lip on the last utterance and flubbed the 
spell.  Her efforts improved her skill in Element Magic.
  The Renegade Swordsman maneuvered to a good defensive position.  Then 
the Renegade Swordsman thrust at Adele with all his strength and inflicted 1 
damage points.  Adele violently assailed the Renegade Swordsman and scored 4 
damage points on the Renegade Swordsman.  The Renegade Swordsman whirled 
around and audaciously swang at Adele and scored on her, doing 4 points of 
damage.  Adele feinted one way, then switched over and viciously swang at 
the Renegade Swordsman and damaged the Renegade Swordsman, inflicting 1 
damage points.
  Adele feigned panic, then pivoted and treacherously thrust at 
the Renegade Swordsman but her aim was just off.  The Renegade Swordsman 
swang at Adele and scorched her with 2 damage points.  Adele forced away 
the Renegade Swordsman with her spirited tactics.  She then swang at 
the Renegade Swordsman with terrific force and inflicted 5 damage points.  
The Renegade Swordsman moved closer and thrust at Adele and inflicted 3 
damage points on her.  Adele was fatally wounded.  Thus did Adele finally 
die, a defiant death by any standard.

  Thy humble servant,   Mortimer, Squire to Adele


From: Indra
To: Bradipo I

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  In my sagely researches, I discovered a fabulous invention 
called the Lead-Lined Helmet!  The following benefits are conferred by the 
Lead-Lined Helmet:
  The Lead-Lined Helmet reduces the effect of a Pyschic Blast spell cast by 
an enemy Psychic from having any effect on any character employed by the 
Kingdom.  The spell will allow only 1-2 free attack rounds.

  Windy spring was followed by a sultry early summer.  I invented nothing 
worthy of note in my sagely researches.
  With the advent of the late summer season I was tutored in Sageness by 
Ishtar.  I rehearsed and practiced my Sageness and improved substantially.
  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained level 6 in Sageness.  All 
characters of this high level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  I invented nothing valuable in my sagely researches.
  With the advent of the fall season, I tried to improve my Sageness, but 
the task seemed beyond my aptitude.  I invented nothing worthy of note in my 
sagely researches.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I invented nothing valuable in 
my sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Indra


